  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1258 PM CDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nRidging remains centered over the Lower Mississippi and Tennessee \nValleys through Wednesday, then shifts further west Thursday before \nextending back towards South Central Texas late week. Triple digit \nheat continues Tuesday for much of the area, then highs ease \nslightly mid to late week, though still remain above normal for mid-\nSeptember. We'll need to keep an eye on heat index values Tuesday \nand possibly Wednesday as they still creep towards the 105-108 \ndegree mark across the I-35 corridor and coastal plains. Rain \nchances remain largely confined to the coastal plains each afternoon \nuntil a potential surge in moisture/PWATs moves across the area \nThursday bringing chances for rain further inland.",
